{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Schemas and Common Schema Objects"}, {"type": "position", "content": 4}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 3}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can use these words when talking about Schema Objects."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Exchange written and spoken information on principles, concepts, data base objects related to query analysis, and data base engines.  Describe relational database, its concepts, and principles in spoken or written texts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses information a wider range of contexts about exchanging technical information on software programming and software solutions, using appropriate grammar and vocabulary at this level. \t  Recognizes simple ideas on concepts on software programming, software solutions and database management."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe7n7le03ob04re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "imply "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to indicate or suggest something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The teacher implied that they might be taken into account for the quiz on Friday."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le03ob04aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "simply "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "in a simple way"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Tables are the first ones, it is simply a basic unit of data storage, they have all the user accessible data, it is divided into columns and rows."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le03ob04aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "owner "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the person who is the proprietor of something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: A schema is just a collection of database objects; it has the name of the user, who is the owner at the same time."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le03ob04aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "several "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "similar to \u201cmany\u201d"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Schema objects can be in different tablespaces, and a tablespace can hold several schemas."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le03ob04aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "topic "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a subject or theme"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I thought you didn't know so much about this topic."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le03ob04aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "retrieval "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the recovery or rescue of information"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Indexes are optional; they are just structures that might be associated with tables, so information retrieval becomes easier."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le03ob04aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I Review the information studied in the lesson"}, {"type": "text", "content": "I design the exam Joe and Mary will answer."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I Make the exam and answer the questions, using the vocabulary and grammar studied. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I Discuss my work with my partners."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Review the information studied in the lesson "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Imagine you are the teacher and design the exam Joe and Mary will answer."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make the exam and answer the questions, using the vocabulary and grammar studied."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Discuss your work with your partners."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Be Supposed to in Questions"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "We use <strong>be supposed to</strong> when we are talking about actions that we expect from people."}, {"type": "text", "content": "We use the especial word combination \"be supposed to\" to talk about actions or events that everyone is expecting to happen.</br></br>  In questions, we use it to confirm information. To use it, we follow this structure: </br></br>  <div class=\"center_text\">Be + subject + supposed to + verb + complement + ?</div> </br></br>  Examples</br> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Are</span> you <span class=\"strong\">supposed to</span> clean all this room alone? That's too much work.</span> </br> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Is</span> she <span class=\"strong\">supposed to</span> be here early? I heard she was late.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Am I supposed to learn all about the schema and schema objects for tomorrow class?  "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Wait, aren't indexes supposed to be tables?"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Passive of Modal Verbs: Might"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "We use the <span class=\"strong\">passive voice</span> when we want to emphasize in the action and not in the person who does it. </br> <span class=\"strong\">Passive voice</span> can be used anytime whener we want focus on the action.This time, we are going to explain how \"might\" is used with <span class=\"strong\">passive voice</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "We use <strong>might</strong> to show possibility or to ask for permission. </br> In <span class=\"strong\">passive voice</span>,  it is the same, but the person behind the action is not important. </br> </br> Structure</br></br> <div class=\"center_text\"> Subject + might be + verb in past participle + complement </div> </br> Examples </br><span class=\"italic\">  Alcoholism <span class=\"strong\">might be considered</span> one of America's biggest problems. </br><span class=\"italic\"> I <span class=\"strong\">might be accepted</span> for that new position at the office.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "The teacher implied that they might be taken into account for the quiz on Friday"}, {"type": "example", "content": "These objects might be confused with the tablespaces, but they are not the same"}, {"type": "example", "content": "they are just structures that might be associated to tables, so information retrieval becomes easier"}], "type": "learning_points"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "welcome", "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"time": "1800", "image": "enpe7n7le03ob04re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<strong>Joe</strong>: Hi, Mary. Quick question: am I supposed to learn all about the schema and schema objects for tomorrow's class?</br>\n<strong>Mary</strong>:  The teacher implied that they might be taken into account for the quiz on Friday. I'm going to review them now, want to join me? </br>\n<strong>Joe</strong>: Sure, thanks a lot. </br>\n<strong>Mary</strong>:  Don't mention it. First, do you know what a schema and schema objects are? </br>"}, {"time": "28000", "image": "enpe7n7le03ob04re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<strong>Joe</strong>: On the one hand, a schema is just a collection of database objects. It has the name of the user, who is the owner at the same time. On the other hand, schema objects are logical structures that refer to database's data. These objects might be confused with the tablespaces, but they are not the same; schema objects can be in different tablespaces, and a tablespace can hold several schemas. </br>\n<strong>Mary</strong>:  I thought you didn't know so much about this topic! </br>\n<strong>Joe</strong>: That's all I know, I have to study the different types of schema objects: tables, indexes, views, clusters, and synonyms.</br>\n<strong>Mary</strong>:  Those are easy! There are five types in total. Tables are simply a basic unit of data storage, they have all the user accessible data, and they are divided into columns and rows.</br>"}, {"time": "89300", "image": "enpe7n7le03ob04re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<strong>Joe</strong>:  Wait a minute! Aren't indexes supposed to be tables?</br>\n<strong>Mary</strong>:  No, they aren't. Indexes are optional; they are just structures that might be associated with tables, so information retrieval becomes easier. The views are supposed to be a kind of table;  they are data presentations, and they hide data complexity and store complex queries. </br>\n<strong>Joe</strong>: What about clusters and synonyms? </br>\n<strong>Mary</strong>:  Clusters are a group of tables that are physically stored on the same disk. It helps to improve the disk access time. Finally, the synonyms are just alias or nicknames that you can give to different types of files; they don't require storage space since they have their definition in the data dictionary."}], "coverimg": "enpe7n7le03ob04re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "enpe7n7le03ob04re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can give a simple definition of schema and schema objects. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can list types of schemas and schema objects. "}, {"type":